From e4c73e1d42fb0b58b3d454ce3f7d38fb0fd63909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:10:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: restore the CX GBIF config on A640 and A680

60a4e18e0e8a ("drm/msm/adreno: Do CX GBIF config before GMU start") moved the
GBIF_QSB_SIDE* programming out of the a640_family branch of hw_init() into a
new catalogue reglist (a640_gbif) that a6xx_gmu_fw_start() applies before the
GMU wakes up.  The list is named after A640, but it was only attached to the
A610/A612, A650, A660, A690, A7xx and A8xx entries - the A640 and A680
(ADRENO_6XX_GEN2) entries were left without it, and the hw_init() branch now
only covers a610_family.  So on every GEN2 part the four QSB side registers
are no longer programmed at all, where pre-7.2 they were written for the
whole a640 family.

On the Xiaomi Book S 12.4 (SC8180X, A680) that leaves the GBIF QoS sides at
whatever the bootloader left behind, and the GPU wedges about a minute into a
GNOME session - A6XX_RBBM_STATUS comes back with the 3D pipeline, VBIF and CP
all busy, the CP stops consuming its ring and the GMU stops answering HFI,
without a single fault/faulting transaction showing up anywhere.

Point both GEN2 entries at the A640 list again, which is exactly the value
pre-7.2 wrote for this family (0x00071620 on QSB_SIDE0..3).
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index 4b46e074d8e2..4c55c9aba4af 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -983,6 +983,7 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
 			.hwcg = a640_hwcg,
 			.protect = &a630_protect,
+			.gbif_cx = a640_gbif,
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00180000,
 		},
@@ -1106,6 +1107,7 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 		.a6xx = &(const struct a6xx_info) {
 			.hwcg = a640_hwcg,
 			.protect = &a630_protect,
+			.gbif_cx = a640_gbif,
 			.gmu_cgc_mode = 0x00020202,
 			.prim_fifo_threshold = 0x00200200,
 		},
